[thin] Nearest-corner classification: these picks join the rear body's outer face to the forward surround's inner end corner across the Y199.75 boundary. They do not measure opposing faces of a finite 1.54 mm wall. Current native sections show the rear section X82.8..91.25 below Z349 and the forward surround X89.75..98.25 above Z349; the rear upper region is open. The corner is where the full silicone-brim bearing ends beside the back-top screw-block passage. Current native face/section coordinates are recorded in the enclosure polish review; the reading does not qualify load capacity or print finish. A ray along each pick's inward normal crosses 8.5 mm or more of material.
alternatives: Treat this as a nearest-corner ranking rather than a wall-thickness measurement. Widening the rear boundary enters the block's 0.25 mm running allowance; trimming below the corner removes part of the required brim bearing. Blending above Z349 behind the seam changes an already empty region.
