[thin] Nominal-section classification: these four 3.000 mm readings cross the nominal 3 mm drain web and front roof-surround wall. The floor readings run from Z0 to Z3; the front-wall readings run between Y-69.092 and Y-66.092 in exported frame coordinates. They identify the ordinary full section. The complete native silicone-brim bearing retains its required 3 mm thickness, as recorded in ../../enclosure/enclosure/y-seam-plain-review.json.
alternatives: Removing material would reduce the ordinary section. Adding stock into the forming clearance or moving the front surround would change the defined funnel fit; the measured nominal section requires no thin-feature allowance.
